-**Observation A: a collapsed edge is detected by its coordinate support.** Suppose \(e=\{i,j\}\in E(G)\). A stress whose only nonzero coordinate is \(w_e=1\) belongs to \(W_G(P)\) if and only if \(p_i=p_j\). Indeed, all equilibrium equations are zero except possibly those at \(i,j\), where the forces are \(p_j-p_i\) and \(p_i-p_j\). Consequently, a collapsed and a noncollapsed realization of this edge cannot have sign-preservingly equivalent \(G\)-fibers: a homeomorphism preserving every coordinate sign would have to preserve the existence of this singleton-support positive stress.
